{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "kjv-titus-002",
  "collection": "kjv-bible",
  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 2,
  "title": "Titus 2",
  "display_title": "Titus 2",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "titus",
  "book": "Titus",
  "bookName": "Titus",
  "bookOrder": 56,
  "testament": "new",
  "chapter": 2,
  "sortOrder": 56002,
  "verseCount": 15,
  "aliases": [
    "Titus",
    "Tit"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:titus:2:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "But speak thou the things which become sound doctrine:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Titus 2:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:2:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:titus:2:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "That the aged men be sober, grave, temperate, sound in faith, in charity, in patience.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Titus 2:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:2:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:titus:2:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "The aged women likewise, that they be in behaviour as becometh holiness, not false accusers, not given to much wine, teachers of good things;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Titus 2:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:2:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:titus:2:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "That they may teach the young women to be sober, to love their husbands, to love their children,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Titus 2:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:2:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:titus:2:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "To be discreet, chaste, keepers at home, good, obedient to their own husbands, that the word of God be not blasphemed.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Titus 2:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:2:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:titus:2:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "Young men likewise exhort to be sober minded.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Titus 2:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:2:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:titus:2:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "In all things shewing thyself a pattern of good works: in doctrine shewing uncorruptness, gravity, sincerity,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Titus 2:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:2:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:titus:2:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "Sound speech, that cannot be condemned; that he that is of the contrary part may be ashamed, having no evil thing to say of you.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Titus 2:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:2:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:titus:2:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "Exhort servants to be obedient unto their own masters, and to please them well in all things; not answering again;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Titus 2:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:2:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:titus:2:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "Not purloining, but shewing all good fidelity; that they may adorn the doctrine of God our Saviour in all things.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Titus 2:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:2:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:titus:2:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "For the grace of God that bringeth salvation hath appeared to all men,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Titus 2:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:2:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:titus:2:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "Teaching us that, denying ungodliness and worldly lusts, we should live soberly, righteously, and godly, in this present world;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Titus 2:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:2:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:titus:2:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "Looking for that blessed hope, and the glorious appearing of the great God and our Saviour Jesus Christ;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Titus 2:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:2:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:titus:2:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "Who gave himself for us, that he might redeem us from all iniquity, and purify unto himself a peculiar people, zealous of good works.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Titus 2:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:2:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:titus:2:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "These things speak, and exhort, and rebuke with all authority. Let no man despise thee.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Titus 2:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:2:15"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
